## Current roadmap / platform inheritance

GitHub #78 and `docs/MESSENGER_PLATFORM_ARCHITECTURE.md` are current authority. Vimla is messenger-first with one backend for Web and future Desktop/Mobile.

Motion rules apply to current Web presentation and later owner-approved design; they do not define native Mobile motion APIs.

# Motion

All interactive components require deliberate hover, focus-visible, pressed, disabled and selected/loading/error states where applicable.

Use shared motion tokens: ~120–140ms fast, ~160–200ms standard, ~220–280ms overlays.

Buttons may use tiny pressed scale. Inputs animate border/ring without layout shift. Menus fade/translate a few pixels. Dialogs fade + subtle scale/translate. Switch/checkbox/tabs animate state.

No exaggerated bounce/glow. Respect prefers-reduced-motion. Functionality must not depend on animation.
